; The refusals of deploy_fixture_preconditions are what keep the deploy arms off an
; operator's own deployment. They read `docker` and `ss` output, so each is driven
; by a stub answering with exactly the holder its case names, and no Docker engine
; is needed. The script's own derivations read two OCaml sources, so those are
; dependencies, at the relative paths the script reads them from.

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (deps
  (:script preconditions.sh)
  ../../scripts/deploy-arms.sh
  ../../lib/common/defaults.ml
  ../../lib/common/builtin_container.ml)
 (action
  (run bash %{script} %{dep:../../scripts/deploy-arms.sh})))
